# playwright-mcp secrets — EXAMPLE
#
# Real secrets live OUTSIDE the repo, at:
#   ~/.config/playwright-mcp/secrets.env          (Linux/macOS)
#   %APPDATA%\playwright-mcp\secrets.env          (Windows)
# (override the path with the PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_SECRETS env var)
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, # for comments, optional quotes. The file is
# passed to the wrapped @playwright/mcp server and read by session_login for
# credential filling. Keep it mode 600; it is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# Credentials for session_login (referenced by credKeys, e.g.
# session_login({ credKeys: { user: "ACME_USER", pass: "ACME_PASS" } })):
ACME_USER=you@example.com
ACME_PASS=replace-me

# session_login also reads the CONSUMING project's ./.env (the project Claude
# Code is running in), or an explicit file via its envFile parameter. When both
# define a key, the project file wins over this user-scoped one. Only the keys
# named in credKeys are ever read.

# Saved authenticated sessions (storageState) are written to, and read from:
#   ~/.config/playwright-mcp/sessions/<name>.json   (mode 600, gitignored)
#   override with PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_SESSIONS

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Remote connector (claude.ai) — PROCESS env vars, set in the service unit /
# container on the VPS (NOT in secrets.env; the server reads process.env). Leave
# ALL of these unset for a normal local install — the server stays stdio-only.
#
# Set ONLY on the remote (VPS) instance. The remote instance is deployed
# SECRETS-FREE: do NOT mount secrets.env or the sessions dir into it (the
# credential-touching tools are denylisted on the remote surface regardless).
#
#   PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_PUBLIC_URL   The public https base URL (the remote ON-SWITCH).
#                               e.g. https://mcp.yourdomain.tld
#   PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_PORT         Local loopback port nginx proxies to (default 8765).
#   PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_BIND         Listen address (default 127.0.0.1). Set to 0.0.0.0
#                               ONLY in a container whose port is NOT host-published
#                               and whose reverse proxy reaches it over the container
#                               network by name (e.g. jstack). Never 0.0.0.0 on a
#                               host that publishes the port to a public interface.
#
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_ID            GitHub OAuth app client id   (proxy-mode OAuth).
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET        GitHub OAuth app client secret  (SENSITIVE).
#   GITHUB_ALLOWED_LOGIN        The ONE GitHub login allowed to use the connector.
#
#   PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_ALLOW_NOAUTH=1   Localhost/dev ONLY — start the remote transport
#                               with NO auth. Never set this on a public host.
#
# Without the GITHUB_* trio (and without ALLOW_NOAUTH), a process that sets
# PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_PUBLIC_URL refuses to start the remote transport (fails closed).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Outbound exfiltration guards (src/exfil.ts) — PROCESS env vars, LOCAL + remote.
# Leave both unset for normal use; the defaults are what you want.
#
# These guard the outbound direction: a malicious page instructing the agent to
# fetch a series of URLs whose paths spell out your private data one character at
# a time (ledger DEC-2026-07-29). Loopback / RFC1918 / .local targets are exempt,
# so debugging local dev servers is never throttled.
#
# Both knobs are deliberately env-only and NOT tool parameters: an injected page
# can talk the model into passing an override argument, but it cannot reach your
# shell. Setting either requires you, at a terminal, then a server restart.
#
#   PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_FETCH_LIMIT      Distinct URLs allowed per registrable domain
#                                   per 10-minute window (default 25). Raise it if
#                                   legitimate bulk traversal of one host is being
#                                   refused — e.g. harvesting a large archive.
#
#   PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_DISABLE_EXFIL_GUARD=1
#                                   Turn the guards OFF entirely — the velocity
#                                   limit, the link-spelling detector, AND the
#                                   outbound secret scan. Diagnostic use only.
